WEBVTT

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:02.469
Subject verb agreement.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:05.959
Find the real subject, and ignore everything in between.

00:00:07.511 --> 00:00:09.261
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:09.261 --> 00:00:15.041
The choices are one verb in different forms, like is and are, or has and have.

00:00:15.041 --> 00:00:18.266
And there are lots of words between the subject and the verb.

00:00:18.266 --> 00:00:19.489
That's on purpose.

00:00:20.526 --> 00:00:24.614
It's testing one thing: whether the verb matches its real subject.

00:00:25.644 --> 00:00:26.919
Here's the method.

00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:30.379
Find the verb blank, and ask: who or what is doing this?

00:00:30.379 --> 00:00:34.649
Cross out the extras: of phrases, and anything between commas.

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:36.474
Look at the subject that's left.

00:00:36.474 --> 00:00:38.834
Is it one thing, or more than one?

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.334
Then match the verb.

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:44.151
Singular verbs usually end in s: is, has, shows.

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:48.469
Rule one: of phrases never change the subject.

00:00:48.469 --> 00:00:50.914
The box of photos were stored is wrong.

00:00:50.914 --> 00:00:52.309
The box was stored.

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:53.370
One box.

00:00:54.439 --> 00:00:57.469
Rule two: two things joined by and are plural.

00:00:57.469 --> 00:00:59.319
So not heat and drought is.

00:00:59.319 --> 00:01:00.630
Heat and drought are.

00:01:01.706 --> 00:01:05.156
Rule three: each, every, and the number of are singular.

00:01:05.156 --> 00:01:07.431
Each of the paintings show is wrong.

00:01:07.431 --> 00:01:08.643
Each one shows.

00:01:09.681 --> 00:01:10.856
Let's try one.

00:01:10.856 --> 00:01:15.506
Cross out the of phrase: of letters written by soldiers during the Civil War.

00:01:15.506 --> 00:01:16.556
What's left?

00:01:16.556 --> 00:01:17.656
The collection.

00:01:17.656 --> 00:01:20.506
That's one thing, so the verb must be singular.

00:01:20.506 --> 00:01:23.866
Offer, have offered, and are offering are all plural.

00:01:23.866 --> 00:01:25.491
Offers is singular.

00:01:25.491 --> 00:01:26.864
The answer is C.

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:29.914
Watch out for the nearest noun.

00:01:29.914 --> 00:01:33.039
The noun right before the verb is usually a decoy.

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:35.939
Items is plural, but it isn't the subject.

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:37.045
The list is.

00:01:38.077 --> 00:01:39.947
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:39.947 --> 00:01:41.007
How to spot it.

00:01:41.007 --> 00:01:42.357
The four steps.

00:01:42.357 --> 00:01:43.462
The rules.

00:01:43.462 --> 00:01:44.487
And the trap.

00:01:44.487 --> 00:01:47.246
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
